  "rules": [
    "Exactly the fixed four cases on the two stated providers, at the specified selected block numbers/hashes. No latest block, discovery, fallback, retry or replacement.",
    "Parent block numbers/hashes are derived solely from saved original block headers. Parent-state unsigned simulations are not labeled original transaction-position replay.",
    "All envelopes come from saved captures, using zero native value and the API current-call profile. No signature generation, signing, submission or paid infrastructure.",
    "Supply/borrow reference quantities are previously recorded same-state provider queries; direct/router quantities and success are unknown and must not be fabricated. A mismatch is evidence to retain, not a reason to rerun.",
    "Capture exact successful HTTP/RPC bodies and hashes. Preserve fixed failure metadata/hashes and count all observed response bytes, including a cap-crossing chunk.",
    "Verify source fingerprint before/after attempts and product identity plus selected state binding in HTTP200 responses. Retain failures and explicit global-limit skips.",
    "The reviewed replay-state runner is adapted only for the fixed current request matrix/route and state identity checks. No production/source edits are authorized by this plan."
  ],
